  },
  {
    "section": "power_ranking_overrides",
    "content": "[\n  {\n    \"team_id\": \"cosmo-wanda-20-pi\",\n    \"trust_score\": 54.0,\n    \"trust_note\": \"Incumbent champion with robust realized velocity (64 closures, +$62.84), but ~$61.79 in open-trade drag continues to offset nearly all booked gains. Trust is held at moderate levels until sustained net equity separation from par is demonstrated.\",\n    \"data_quality\": \"Official\",\n    \"data_quality_note\": \"Continuous official-tier feed. Realized data is robust; live unrealized marks remain volatile and unverified as booked profit.\",\n    \"interesting_discoveries\": \"Generates the highest realized velocity (~$1.14/hr) yet ends with below-par equity, indicating Top 20 scalping frequency may be subsidizing larger adverse swing positions. The realized-to-equity gap is the widest in the league.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"team_id\": \"timmy-20-pc\",\n    \"trust_score\": 19.0,\n    \"trust_note\": \"Leads nominal equity at ~$1,002.06, but only ~$0.29 is realized with ~$16.03 locked in a single open position. Trust remains speculative until repeatable closure discipline is demonstrated across a larger sample.\",\n    \"data_quality\": \"Clean\",\n    \"data_quality_note\": \"100% scheduled uptime with no restarts, yet a single closed trade renders rate-based projections unreliable per system sample flags.\",\n    \"interesting_discoveries\": \"Economic exposure is effectively binary: one open trade determines league-leading equity. A reversal could push the strategy below par without ever having posted a material realized win, revealing extreme concentration risk.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"team_id\": \"cosmo-wanda-50-pc\",\n    \"trust_score\": 26.0,\n    \"trust_note\": \"Post-restart challenger with healthy realized scalps (16 trades, +$12.57) but ~$29.42 in unrealized drag across six open positions. Trust is reduced until restart backfill is verified and open bleed is meaningfully reduced.\",\n    \"data_quality\": \"Restarted\",\n    \"data_quality_note\": \"Runtime continuity is provisional following a restart. Realized trade count is healthy, but economic risk is concentrated in adverse marks that may reflect restart-state misalignment.\",\n    \"interesting_discoveries\": \"Despite a 100% realized win rate, raw total PnL is negative (~-$16.85), implying Top 50 breadth produces frequent small winners while larger losing accumulations build off-book. This raises structural questions about whether expanded pair coverage preserves risk-adjusted returns or merely dilutes edge with noise.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"team_id\": \"timmy-50-pc\",\n    \"trust_score\": 16.0,\n    \"trust_note\": \"The only competitor with booked realized losses (-$19.81, 1W/2L) and below-par equity (~$980.19). After ~57 hours, Top 50 breadth has not produced a profitable realized sequence; coverage expansion appears to be introducing adverse selection rather than alpha.\",\n    \"data_quality\": \"Clean\",\n    \"data_quality_note\": \"Uninterrupted runtime with no restarts, yet only three closed trades keep risk-adjusted metrics flagged as projection-unreliable.\",\n    \"interesting_discoveries\": \"Timmy-50 booked immediate realized losses while Timmy-20 avoided losses entirely by deferring closure. This divergence suggests Top 50 noise may force earlier unfavorable exits or that signal decay is faster across the expanded universe, undermining the strategy's core premise.\"\n  }\n]",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-08T07:44:46.948863+00:00"
  },
